PROJECT DOCUMENTATION

1. Project Initialization
The Spring Boot application was created using Maven with Java 21.
Core modules included:
Spring Web
Spring Data JPA
Spring Security
MySQL Connector
Lombok
This established the foundation for our chat application's backend.

2. Database Connection Setup
Configured application.properties to connect the backend to a MySQL database.
Verified successful startup logs and ensured Hibernate created necessary tables.

3. User Entity & Repository Creation
Developed the User entity with fields:
id
username
password
Implemented UserRepository extending JpaRepository to perform CRUD and queries.

4. User Registration API Implementation
Created a clean registration flow under /api/auth/register:
Validates incoming data
Ensures username is unique
Saves a new user to the database
Returns the registered user as a JSON response
Successfully tested using Postman.

5. Initial Security Configuration
Added a basic SecurityConfig to:
Disable CSRF for APIs
Permit access to /api/auth/** (login, register)
Restrict all other endpoints
Disable form login
Use stateless API-style authentication
This was preparation for JWT-based security.

6. JWT (JSON Web Token) Integration Setup
Installed jjwt dependencies and implemented:
JwtUtil class
Token generation logic
Token validation and claim parsing
Expiry timestamp handling
This established the authentication mechanism for session-less communication.

7. Login Endpoint With JWT Token Generation
Implemented /api/auth/login API:
Validates username and password
Checks credentials against database
Generates a signed JWT token
Returns token to the client
This token is essential for accessing secured API endpoints.

8. JWT Authentication Filter
Created a custom filter to:
Intercept incoming requests
Read the Authorization header
Validate the JWT token
Extract username from token
Set authentication inside Spring Security
This enables seamless token-based authentication for protected routes.

9. Updated SecurityConfig With JWT Integration
Integrated the JWT filter into Spring Security:
Added filter before UsernamePasswordAuthenticationFilter
Switched authentication mode to fully stateless
Ensured protected routes require a valid JWT token
This completed the full authentication pipeline.

10. API Testing With Postman
Performed verification for:
Register → Success
Login → Returns valid JWT
Protected endpoints:
Access without token → 401 Unauthorized
Access with token → Successfully authorized